# CLAUDE.md section 17: "binary artifacts are force-added so each lesson reproduces
# from the repo". The embedding caches used to be excluded here (`*.npz`), and
# `git ls-files` confirmed none was tracked -- so no cloner could reproduce a single
# number in the README without a GPU re-embed. That exclusion is REMOVED.
#
# TRACK (force-add): artifacts/seqs_<condition>_<embedder>.npz -- the ragged per-turn
# embedding packs. Each now carries a CONTENT FINGERPRINT (embed.content_fingerprint),
# so a tracked cache is verifiable rather than merely present. Sizes measured on this
# host: MiniLM 2.5-2.9 MB each, Gemma-3-1B (1152-d) 7.4-8.6 MB each; EmbeddingGemma
# (768-d) lands between the two. Every number in results.json is re-derivable on CPU
# from these packs alone.
#
# Nothing is ignored here. If a future artifact is genuinely too large to track, add
# it BY NAME with the measured size and the regeneration command, never a wildcard.
